# Icewrought Sentry: the second ability only triggers when you tap an untapped creature an opponent controls (CR 701.26a: a
# permanent that is already tapped cannot be tapped, so nothing is tapped). Turn 4: Bot2 taps its Llanowar Elves for mana, and it
# stays tapped through turn 5. Bot1 attacks with the Sentry and pays {1}{U}; the reflexive trigger targets the tapped Elves and does
# nothing, so the Sentry stays 2/3 and deals 2 (20 - 2 = 18).

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Sapphire
Mox Sapphire
Icewrought Sentry
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Icewrought Sentry.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Activate
? Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Tapped = true
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Icewrought Sentry > Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire#2.Activate
Bot1.PayCost
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T5 Bot1.Main2]

